    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "62eac7a2cd9e2d887059b5853d249bb61d767b05670b067f71d53b5b94a088f8",
      "text": "Day 5 · Breakfast, then a group tour with an English-speaking guide to the restored Ahu Akivi, in the centre of the island, whose seven Moai are said to represent the seven explorers sent to Rapa Nui by King Hotu Matua; the unrestored Ahu Hanga Puku Riki; and Puna Pau, the green, picturesque quarry whose red tuff was used for the Moai’s topknots. End at the ceremonial complex of Tahai, with its three platforms, Ko Te Riku (with restored eyes), Tahai and Vai Ure, part of Rapa Nui National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Transfer to the airport for your flight to Santiago; on arrival, transfer to the hotel.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "18SzywAPCgdKEUPkYKDL05UCtQOGhj0Ob",
        "documentSha256": "5ad921988e8413d36aee91207a7e895c91209d186124ccf72d0324c033d3ee8e",
